### case-service — example requests
# case/case-service-with-loco — loco-idiomatic layout (src/controllers/).
# Envelope: BARE loco JSON — curl-verified identical posture to
# organization/care-pathway, NOT the "{success,data,error}" shape a
# stale doc note once suggested (see examples/api/README.md). Gated by
# CASE_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off).
#
# GOTCHA (curl-verified): case has NO `GET /review-queue` HTTP surface
# (unlike organization/care-pathway) — bulk import still routes likely
# duplicates into the `review_queue` table (bulk-import-export.md),
# there is just no REST endpoint to list/decide them yet. Hitting a
# made-up `/api/cases/review-queue` doesn't 404 — it matches the
# `{pid}` route and 500s trying to parse "review-queue" as a UUID
# ("invalid character: found `r` at 0"). Don't copy that path.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8089
@casePid = REPLACE_WITH_PID_FROM_CREATE
# curl-verified example: creating the body below in a local run produced
# pid a00bd500-f953-434d-ab8b-ee35eabacb67 — copy your own create
# response's "pid" instead of reusing this one.
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/_health


### Who am I — always requires a valid bearer token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create a case — minimal valid body.
# curl-verified response: {"pid":"<uuid>","title":"Housing benefit appeal"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cases
Content-Type: application/json
Accepts-version: 1.0

{
  "title": "Housing benefit appeal",
  "agency_id": "dwp",
  "case_number": "HB-2024-0007",
  "subjects": ["person:abc"],
  "keywords": ["housing", "benefit"],
  "identifiers": [{ "scheme": "Docket", "value": "CV-2024-001234" }]
}


### Get the created case back. If the ABAC policy's deciding allow rule
# carries a `mask` obligation, this transparently returns mask_case(...)
# instead — curl-verified shape: case_number/subjects/identifiers/
# same_as zeroed, everything else intact
# (agents/share/authorization-attributes.md §11; no-op with
# CASE_REQUIRE_AUTH off, as in this compose).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/{{casePid}}


### List — paginated (curl-verified X-Total-Count/X-Limit/X-Offset headers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases?limit=25&offset=0


### Search — fuzzy + phonetic via Tantivy; title/subjects/agency/identifiers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/search?q=Housing&fuzzy=true


### Update a case
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/{{casePid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Housing benefit appeal (amended)",
  "agency_id": "dwp",
  "case_number": "HB-2024-0007",
  "status": "in_progress"
}


### Probabilistic + deterministic match
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/match
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Housing benefit appeal", "agency_id": "dwp" }


### Explicit duplicate check — curl-verified: bare `[]` when no candidates
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/check-duplicates
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Housing benefit appeal" }


### Merge two confirmed-duplicate cases (destructive)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/merge
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "main_pid": "{{casePid}}", "duplicate_pid": "<other-uuid>" }


### Recent merges
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/merges/recent


### Cross-service link — assert this case is `subject_of` a person
# (the highest-governance v1 edge kind, cross-service-linking.md §10;
# case is the crate that originates this edge).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/{{casePid}}/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "subject_of",
  "to_ref": "person:11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "provenance": "operator"
}


### List this case's outbound links
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/{{casePid}}/links


### Bulk edge pull for the link-graph aggregator's reconciliation
# (a privileged/governed read — cross-service-linking.md §8)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/links?since=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z


### Always-masked view (privacy.md — distinct from the obligation-driven
# mask on the plain GET above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/{{casePid}}/masked


### GDPR export
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/{{casePid}}/export


### Audit trail for this record
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/{{casePid}}/audit


### Recent audit log (system-wide) — curl-verified: hash-chained rows
# (prev_hash/hash/hash_sha3, agents/share/auditability.md)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/audit/recent


### Bulk import (JSONL/CSV) — 202 Accepted, returns a job id
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/import
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "format": "jsonl", "dedupe_mode": "upsert" }


### Bulk export
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/export
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "format": "csv" }


### FHIR R5 — read this case as a Task resource (governmental case ⇒
# Task, the documented best-effort mapping, agents/share/fhir.md §3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/fhir/Task/{{casePid}}


### Delete (soft-delete) a case
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/cases/{{casePid}}
